verdict.merge_risk:
Code risk is low:
- one post-plan pass, run once per movement plan in round 1;
- three `not rc_going` guards in the NORMAL MOVE branch;
- one new static (reset in reset_caches);
- FIX_RANGED_CENTRE=0 skips the pass, and with required change 7 the base is byte-exact;
- cost is negligible: units x models once per plan;
- all code hunks apply on 1.56.8 (constants hunk by hand); no interaction with WAAAGH-ADV-CHARGE (chase gate) or the parked R1-* fixes.

Main risks:
1. It will almost certainly be PARKED by the V2-1 fix gate. No weapon in the three bench lists has [HEAVY], so the Heavy branch is dead there. The corridor branch can only reach Prosecutors and Warbikers A/B, and the designer's Orks pair had 0 fires. Do not widen the trigger to gain reach: non-Lootas blockers going to the centre are unmeasured, and the centre-guarding blocks were neutral.
2. The evidence is narrow. Three clear findings, all in the Orks mirror, all one-round rollouts, with horizon 2 still pending. In Orks vs Custodes, every measured Lootas-to-centre alternative was neutral or harmful (s7490 -3.83, s7470 -5.50). There the not-alone and threat guards are the only protection, and that is unmeasured.
3. F1 is reproduced by the sibling unit (Gamma), not the measured Alpha. Its value rests on 1 seed until the extra check runs.
4. Later rounds are not priced: a 10-model W1 Lootas unit stands in the open centre in rounds 2-3, and the opponent can score kill cards. The round-1 gate and the forward bias avoid the round-2 FAR_TRIP/OVERCOMMIT hold-back failure, but not this exposure.
5. Rules-fidelity context for V2-4, not this fix. T7-26 holds the unit still (10e reading). The engine applies the 11e Heavy +1 when no model moved more than 3\" (ModifierStack.heavy_applies_11e), and T7-26's 'reachable this turn' test measures centroid to marker, not the 11e hosting area. Correcting either changes which units count as Heavy-idle, so re-run the decision checks after any V2-4 change to T7-26 or RACE-1.

At ship time only (if it ever clears V2-2): add the version_history.json entry and a windowed scenario, per the project rules.
